.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt VINIT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vinit
.Nd small init and service supervisor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs as process 1.
It mounts the API filesystems, starts every service defined in
.Pa /etc/vinit/services ,
supervises them, reaps orphaned processes and shuts the system down.
It takes commands from
.Xr vinitctl 8
over a Unix socket.
.Pp
To boot with
.Nm ,
add
.Ql init=/usr/bin/vinit
to the kernel command line.
.Nm
refuses to run as any process other than 1.
.Ss Boot
.Nm
mounts
.Pa /proc ,
.Pa /sys ,
.Pa /dev ,
.Pa /dev/pts ,
.Pa /dev/shm
and
.Pa /run
if they are not mounted yet.
Then it reads every
.Pa *.conf
file in
.Pa /etc/vinit/services ,
checks dependencies and starts all services in dependency order.
.Xr vinit.conf 5
describes the file format.
A file that is invalid marks its service failed; the other services
still start.
.Ss Supervision
Each service runs in its own session, so its process group holds
everything it starts.
With cgroup v2, each service also runs in its own cgroup,
.Ar name Ns Pa .service ,
next to
.Pa init.scope ,
which holds
.Nm
itself.
Stop signals go to every process in the cgroup, so a process that leaves
its process group cannot escape.
.Nm
mounts cgroup v2 on
.Pa /sys/fs/cgroup
if it is not mounted yet.
When a service exits,
.Nm
applies its restart policy with exponential backoff.
Readiness notification follows the s6 protocol: the service writes a
newline to a file descriptor.
.Ss Shutdown
On shutdown,
.Nm
stops services in reverse dependency order.
It sends
.Dv SIGTERM
to each process group, then
.Dv SIGKILL
after the stop timeout.
Then it runs
.Pa /etc/vinit/shutdown
with the argument
.Cm reboot ,
.Cm poweroff
or
.Cm halt ,
if that file is executable.
Last, it kills all remaining processes, turns off swap, unmounts all
filesystems, remounts
.Pa /
read-only and reboots, powers off or halts.
.Ss Emergency shell
.Nm
starts
.Pa /bin/sh
on the console if no service file is usable, or if a service with
.Cm critical = yes
fails.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM, SIGINT"
.It Dv SIGTERM , SIGINT
Reboot.
The kernel sends
.Dv SIGINT
on Ctrl-Alt-Del.
.It Dv SIGUSR1
Halt.
.It Dv SIGUSR2
Power off.
.El
.Pp
These are the signals that busybox
.Xr reboot 8 ,
.Xr halt 8
and
.Xr poweroff 8
send.
.Sh KERNEL COMMAND LINE
.Bl -tag -width vinit.quiet
.It Cm vinit.quiet
Print only warnings and errors on the console.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Services get only
.Ev PATH ,
.Ev TERM
and the variables set with
.Cm env
in their service file.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/vinit/services -compact
.It Pa /etc/vinit/services
Service files.
.It Pa /etc/vinit/shutdown
Optional shutdown hook.
.It Pa /run/vinit/control
Control socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vinit.conf 5 ,
.Xr vinitctl 8
.Sh BUGS
.Nm
is experimental.
It has had no independent security review and no use on real hardware.
